## Permitted Purpose

A permitted purpose is any purpose other than a commercial
purpose.

A commercial purpose is any purpose where you or another
party receives or expects to receive any direct or indirect
financial, monetary, or commercial benefit, compensation,
or advantage from using, distributing, white-labeling,
reselling, or providing the software (or any modified or
hosted version of it) as a product or service.

For clarity, you may **not**:
- Clone, rebrand, white-label, or customize the software
  to sell, license, or distribute it for profit; or
- Offer the software (original or modified) as a paid
  hosted service, SaaS, or commercial offering without a
  separate written commercial license from the licensor.

You **may**:
- Clone, study, customize, and self-host the software for
  personal, educational, or non-commercial use; and
- Contribute improvements, bug fixes, and features back
  to the project.

